# FSOC launcher — non-secret local defaults (optional).
#
# Copy this file to `fsoc.env` (gitignored) and edit it if you want to skip
# the interactive prompts in ./run_fsoc.sh. No file here is required for
# basic use -- every value below has a sensible interactive fallback.
#
# Never put secrets in this file — there is nothing secret to configure for
# FSOC (no API keys, no credentials).

# Default camera index for "Phone Camera Demo" / "Golden Phone Demo"
# (run ./run_fsoc.sh probe to see what's actually available on your machine).
#FSOC_CAMERA_INDEX=0

# Path to your camera calibration file (see docs/PHONE_CAMERA_METRICS.md
# "Camera calibration"). Personal / hardware-specific -- never commit one.
#FSOC_CAMERA_CALIBRATION=configs/phone_camera.cfg

# Path to the TinyBeaconNet ONNX model for Hybrid/AI perception in phone-
# camera mode. Defaults to the committed model if this is unset.
#FSOC_AI_MODEL=models/tiny_beacon_net.onnx

# NOTE on the frontend port: it is NOT configurable here. The launcher reads
# it directly from frontend/package.json's own `-p` flag (currently 4317) so
# it can never drift from what next actually does -- change it there if you
# need a different port.
